Subject: Use full script paths and per run temp dir for kanban workers

Why: Kanban workers start in `/opt/data/kanban/workspaces/<task-id>` where relative `scripts/*.py` paths fail with `No such file or directory`, and concurrent workers share `/tmp` so fixed `/tmp/kueue-logs` and `/tmp/kueue-ledger.json` paths race across sessions (`agents/platform/AGENTS.md`). Invoking scripts by their full `/opt/data/profiles/platform/skills/gke-kueue-troubleshooting/scripts/<name>.py` path with literal `python3` and using a per-run `mktemp -d /tmp/kueue-triage.XXXXXX` directory fixes both.
Local-Issue: none (adoption of gke-kueue-troubleshooting from google/skills)
Eval-Case: kueue-troubleshooting-mixed-flavor-tas-probe
Upstream-Issue: none (specific to this repository)
Retire-When: never; the platform profile script path and shared-sandbox temp-dir rules are this repository's

